---
description: Never wipe IndexedDB or LocalStorage on schema version bumps
alwaysApply: true
---

# Persistence safety

- Schema version bumps are additive. Never `clear`, `del`, or reset IndexedDB/LocalStorage during a migration.
- `clearAllData` is user-initiated only (backup UI). Migrations must not call it.
- If stored `transactions` is an array, never persist `[]` over it. Keep rows that pass `isTransaction`.
- Write the new `schemaVersion` without rewriting the transactions key unless a real transform ran.
- New entity fields stay optional so `isTransaction` does not drop legacy rows.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — version bump empties the ledger
if (schemaVersion < CURRENT) {
  await del(KEYS.transactions);
  await set(KEYS.schemaVersion, CURRENT);
}

// ✅ GOOD — bump version, keep the array
const transactions = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw.filter(isTransaction) : [];
await set(KEYS.schemaVersion, CURRENT);
```
